1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,103
This town is in the United States,

2
00:00:02,103 --> 00:00:03,502
but you can't drive there

3
00:00:03,502 --> 00:00:05,800
without leaving the United States.

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,336
This is Point Roberts, Washington.

5
00:00:08,336 --> 00:00:10,350
About 13 square kilometres,

6
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,000
and 1,200 people.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,238
In 1846, Britain and America

8
00:00:14,238 --> 00:00:17,434
split this region along a straight line:

9
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,200
the 49th parallel.

10
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:21,410
The line didn't care about the coast.

11
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:23,739
It sliced right through this peninsula,

12
00:00:23,739 --> 00:00:26,400
and left its tip on the American side.

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,032
So to reach the rest of America by land,

14
00:00:29,032 --> 00:00:31,466
you drive about 40 km through Canada,

15
00:00:31,466 --> 00:00:33,600
and cross the border twice.

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,954
Older kids have long taken a school bus through Canada:

17
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:39,800
four border crossings, every school day.

18
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,812
And when the border shut in 2020,

19
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:43,885
the whole town was cut off by land

20
00:00:43,885 --> 00:00:45,981
for over a year and a half.

21
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,338
Would you live in an American town where

22
00:00:48,338 --> 00:00:51,477
you need a passport to go shopping in America?
